⏺ I added imports to the bottom of main.py for all 16 @app-decorated functions
  in views/ (meetings, notes, tasks and users). I checked it by importing main:
  all 16 routes now register on app, along with the existing / route.

  Why the imports are at the bottom: each views module runs from main import 
  app, so the imports have to come after app = FastAPI(...). Putting them at the
  top would cause a circular import that fails. A comment in the file explains
  this, and # noqa: E402, F401 stops linters from flagging the late placement
  and the names that look unused.

  This works when the app is started with uvicorn main:app. It won't work if
  main.py is run directly with python main.py: the file then runs as __main__,
  so the views import a second copy of main and attach their routes to a
  different app.

  A cleaner long-term setup would give each view file its own APIRouter and
  register them in main.py with app.include_router(...). That removes the
  circular dependency entirely. I can make that change if you'd like.

