⏺ I switched the views to APIRouter, which removes the circular import.

  - Each file in views/ now creates its own router = APIRouter() and uses
    @router.get/post/... instead of @app.... They no longer import anything from
    main.
  - main.py imports the four view modules at the top and registers each one with
    app.include_router(...). The block of per-function imports from the
    previous step is gone.

  Importing main registers all 16 view routes, and uvicorn main:app works as
  before. Running python main.py directly no longer causes a problem either. I
  didn't commit anything.

  I left the full paths (like "/users/") in each decorator, so the routes are
  unchanged. If you want, I can move the path parts into
  APIRouter(prefix="/users", tags=["users"]) instead, which would also group the
  endpoints by resource in /docs.

