⏺ I added a middleware that reads the user id from an X-User-ID request header
  and passes it to every view. The header name was my choice since you didn't
  specify one.

  - middleware.py (new file):
    - UserIdMiddleware reads the header and saves it as request.state.user_id.
      If the value isn't an integer, it returns a 400. If the header is missing,
      it saves None.
    - get_current_user_id is a small dependency that gives the id to a view, or
      returns a 401 if there isn't one. I put this check in the dependency
      rather than the middleware so /, /docs and /openapi.json still work
      without the header.
  - main.py registers the middleware with app.add_middleware(UserIdMiddleware).
  - Each view now takes current_user_id: int = Depends(get_current_user_id). I
    named it current_user_id because get_user already has a user_id path
    parameter. The views receive the id but don't use it yet.

  I ran it with uvicorn and tested with curl:

  ┌────────────────────────────────────────┬────────┐
  │                Request                 │ Status │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────┼────────┤
  │ / without the header                   │ 200    │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────┼────────┤
  │ /users/ without the header             │ 401    │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────┼────────┤
  │ /users/ with X-User-ID: abc            │ 400    │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────┼────────┤
  │ /users/ and /users/3 with X-User-ID: 7 │ 200    │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────┼────────┤
  │ /docs                                  │ 200    │
  └────────────────────────────────────────┴────────┘

  I couldn't use FastAPI's TestClient because httpx isn't installed.

  Decisions for you:
  - Creating a user needs the header too. POST /users/ currently requires a user
    id. If that should work without one (for sign-up), I can exempt that route.
  - Swagger UI has no field for the header. Adding an APIKeyHeader security
    scheme would give /docs an "Authorize" button for setting it.

