⏺ A few access rules need deciding first. Meetings currently have no owner, so
  I'll make these choices and you can change any of them:

  - Meetings get a new owner_id column, set to whoever created the meeting. You
    can see and update a meeting if you own it or attend it. Only the owner can
    delete it; anyone else gets 403.
  - Notes and tasks follow their meeting: you can access them only if you can
    access that meeting.
  - Users: you can see yourself and anyone you share a meeting with. You can
    still add any existing user as an attendee by id; otherwise you couldn't
    invite anyone.
  - POST /users/ works without the header. Every other endpoint returns 401 if
    the header is missing or names a user that doesn't exist.

