  For item 6, the Transport interface and LocalTransport exist, but there's no
  setting that picks a transport. Each mesh also holds a database session from
  the request, which a remote transport couldn't send to another machine. Errors
  (NotFoundError and the others) would also need to be packed up and rebuilt on
  the calling side.

  Pending actions

  Remaining requirements
  1. Caching in the mesh. Cache reads per user, and clear them on create, update
     and delete, including results that depend on other services (for example,
     changing a meeting's attendees changes who can see which users).
  2. The get_tools() decorator. It would mark which service methods are exposed
     and build tool definitions (name, description, input schema) from their
     signatures and docstrings. The tools would need to run through the
     user-specific mesh so access rules still apply.
  3. Make transports configurable. Pick the transport from a setting such as an
     environment variable, and move the database session into the in-process
     setup so the mesh itself doesn't depend on it.

