  How values are loaded
  - Overrides: any setting can be changed with an environment variable of the
    same name in capitals, or with a .env file in the project root. Environment
    variables take priority over the file. .env is already in .gitignore.
  - MESH_BACKEND works exactly as before.
  - Bad values fail at startup: for example, MESH_BACKEND=postgres stops the app
    with a message saying the value must be sqlite or memory.
  - One shared copy: main.py, database.py and middleware.py all read from a
    single settings object.

